d3d12: Stage CPU-written buffers in write-back memory on UMA

On a UMA device, buffers the CPU writes, texture upload staging among
them, went in D3D12_HEAP_TYPE_UPLOAD, write-combined memory. WSL2's GPU
paravirtualization maps that memory uncached: writing it ran at 383 MB/s
against 13049 MB/s for write-back memory on a Radeon 780M, which does not
report CacheCoherentUMA, so a 1080p glTexSubImage2D took 25 ms and a
video's frames kept a core three quarters busy.

Give them a custom heap with write-back CPU pages in L0, as readback
buffers have and as Dozen's host-cached memory type does.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_bufmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_bufmgr.cpp
@@ -144,6 +144,18 @@
       d3d12_evicted : d3d12_resident;
 
    D3D12_HEAP_PROPERTIES heap_pris = GetCustomHeapProperties(dev, heap_type);
+   /* On a UMA device, CPU-written buffers, texture upload staging among
+    * them, live in write-back memory as readback ones do, and as Dozen's
+    * host-cached memory type does. Write-combined memory is mapped uncached
+    * under WSL2's GPU paravirtualization, where writing it ran 34 times slower
+    * (383 against 13049 MB/s on a Radeon 780M, which does not report
+    * CacheCoherentUMA), and a 1080p glTexSubImage2D took 25 ms.
+    */
+   if (heap_type == D3D12_HEAP_TYPE_UPLOAD && screen->architecture.UMA) {
+      heap_pris.Type = D3D12_HEAP_TYPE_CUSTOM;
+      heap_pris.CPUPageProperty = D3D12_CPU_PAGE_PROPERTY_WRITE_BACK;
+      heap_pris.MemoryPoolPreference = D3D12_MEMORY_POOL_L0;
+   }
    d3d12_screen_reclaim_completed(screen);
    HRESULT hres;
    do {
